From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: report 32_BIT_ONLY denorm independence on Valhall
 biblioklept

Valhall (v9+) selects flush-to-zero with one 2-bit field per shader in
the shader program descriptor (Preserve, DX11, Always, Abrupt) and has
no per-instruction FTZ for ALU ops; the compiler only derives that
field from float_controls_execution_mode (pan_shader_info ftz_fp16 /
ftz_fp32, shader_ftz_mode). DX11 flushes FP32 and preserves FP16, so
FP32 can be preserved or flushed independently of FP16. "Flush FP16,
preserve FP32" does not exist, and FP16 and FP64 cannot be set apart.

Report denormBehaviorIndependence = 32_BIT_ONLY on v9+ and stop
reporting shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat16/64 (preserve stays true for
all three, FP32 reports both). The only combinations a shader can then
request are the ones the descriptor can express, which unblocks
vkd3d-proton SM6.2 (needs independence != NONE plus FP32 flush and
preserve; native 16-bit needs FP16 preserve). Update the pan_compiler
comment accordingly.

Build-only; not device-tested. The DX11-preserves-FP16 behaviour is
taken from the compiler and descriptor use; run
dEQP-VK.spirv_assembly.instruction.*.float_controls.* on a v10+ device
before release and revert to NONE if the mixed FP16/FP32 cases fail.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.c           |    7 ++++---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c |   12 +++++++++---
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.c
index 8c99ff4..ceb972c 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/pan_compiler.c
@@ -355,9 +355,10 @@ pan_shader_update_info(struct pan_shader_info *info, nir_shader *s,
 
    if (arch >= 9) {
       /* Valhall hardware doesn't have a "flush FP16, preserve FP32" mode, and
-       * we don't advertise independent FP16/FP32 denorm modes in panvk, but
-       * it's still possible to have shaders that don't specify any denorm mode
-       * for FP32. In that case, default to flush FP32. */
+       * panvk only reports FP32 as independent (FP16 flush-to-zero is not
+       * advertised), but it's still possible to have shaders that don't
+       * specify any denorm mode for FP32. In that case, default to flush
+       * FP32. */
       if (info->ftz_fp16 && !info->ftz_fp32) {
          assert(!nir_is_denorm_preserve(execution_mode, 32));
          info->ftz_fp32 = true;
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
index 802118c..2bbe741 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_physical_device.c
@@ -1093,8 +1093,14 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_properties)(
       /* VK_KHR_driver_properties */
       .driverID = VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_PANVK,
       .conformanceVersion = get_conformance_version(),
+      /* Valhall has one 2-bit flush-to-zero mode per shader (Preserve, DX11
+       * = FP32 flushed and FP16 preserved, Always = both flushed) and no
+       * per-instruction override, so only FP32 can differ from the 16/64-bit
+       * types, and "flush FP16, preserve FP32" does not exist.
+       * shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat16/64 are therefore not reported.
+       */
       .denormBehaviorIndependence =
-         PAN_ARCH >= 9 ? VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_NONE
+         PAN_ARCH >= 9 ? VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_32_BIT_ONLY
                        : VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_ALL,
       .roundingModeIndependence = VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_ALL,
       .shaderSignedZeroInfNanPreserveFloat16 = true,
@@ -1103,9 +1109,9 @@ panvk_per_arch(get_physical_device_properties)(
       .shaderDenormPreserveFloat16 = true,
       .shaderDenormPreserveFloat32 = true,
       .shaderDenormPreserveFloat64 = true,
-      .shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat16 = true,
+      .shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat16 = PAN_ARCH < 9,
       .shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat32 = true,
-      .shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat64 = true,
+      .shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat64 = PAN_ARCH < 9,
       .shaderRoundingModeRTEFloat16 = true,
       .shaderRoundingModeRTEFloat32 = true,
       .shaderRoundingModeRTEFloat64 = false,
